(7464633, 1184059, 30982, '<td valign="top">Yikes!  Scares the livin'' daylights outta me!  We''ve had so many big fires already this season... Yikes!!  But it makes for a WAY cool picture.  I like the take of having the second person in the shot, too.<br/> <br/>Sad to hear of your mother in law passing.</td>', 'Yikes!  Scares the livin'' daylights outta me!  We''ve had so many big fires already this season... Yikes!!  But it makes for a WAY cool picture.  I like the take of having the second person in the shot, too. Sad to hear of your mother in law passing.', '2016-07-15 23:11:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(7464638, 1184059, 86447, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Melethia:</b></div><hr/><i> Yikes!  Scares the livin'' daylights outta me!  We''ve had so many big fires already this season... Yikes!!  But it makes for a WAY cool picture.  I like the take of having the second person in the shot, too.<br/> <br/>Sad to hear of your mother in law passing. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Not to worry, Deb. <br/> <br/>It had rained here a couple of hours before. <br/> <br/>My shoes were wet when I got inside. <br/> <br/>I live with a Safety Police ( self appointed) , so there was no chance of me doing something dangerous. *rolleyes*<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Melethia: Yikes!  Scares the livin'' daylights outta me!  We''ve had so many big fires already this season... Yikes!!  But it makes for a WAY cool picture.  I like the take of having the second person in the shot, too. Sad to hear of your mother in law passing.   Not to worry, Deb.  It had rained here a couple of hours before.  My shoes were wet when I got inside.  I live with a Safety Police ( self appointed) , so there was no chance of me doing something dangerous. *rolleyes*', '2016-07-16 00:44:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(7465881, 1183871, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Ouch, coming in 2nd from last...been there, done that, not much fun.  I think in this instance you may not have realize what ''painting with light'' is, and when you look at the homepage you realize it''s the controlled use of light to enhance a subject, whether it is with a flashlight or tiny LEDs.<br/> <br/>Still this is quite a good cityscape-at-sunset shot, and I do find my eye going from the neon sign to the tree on the right and then up to the setting sun.  It has a dreamy feel to it, but sadly not a painted light feel :-/  This is one of those learning-curve challenges, so hopefully next time a painted light challenge is announced you have an idea as to what to shoot for.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps, please keep shooting and entering!<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Ouch, coming in 2nd from last...been there, done that, not much fun.  I think in this instance you may not have realize what ''painting with light'' is, and when you look at the homepage you realize it''s the controlled use of light to enhance a subject, whether it is with a flashlight or tiny LEDs. Still this is quite a good cityscape-at-sunset shot, and I do find my eye going from the neon sign to the tree on the right and then up to the setting sun.  It has a dreamy feel to it, but sadly not a painted light feel :-/  This is one of those learning-curve challenges, so hopefully next time a painted light challenge is announced you have an idea as to what to shoot for. Hope this helps, please keep shooting and entering! Susan', '2016-07-25 23:10:05.000000', NULL, 0),
